{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"cfff77422ccf0f18c3b5a4e3cf13d740bfdf5f2c4352f26e6bcc13126f8f7141","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T21:54:27Z","payload":{"action":"dismissed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_recovered_from":"c9c8a905f98e1b692a1b0264c2072d57eefba163a815f7197401449f8d842bf2","anchor_verified":true,"mapped_intervals":[[84,84]],"mapped_path":".github/workflows/ratchet-propose.yml","reason":"The premise is wrong: GitHub Actions' workflow-run object exposes `path` as the bare workflow file path (for example `.github/workflows/main.yml`); the `@main` / `@refs/heads/main` suffix belongs to workflow-ref forms, not `run.path`. The exact comparison at line 84 therefore matches the API value, and the current contract contains no requirement to accept a suffixed path.","recovered_anchor":{"anchor_recovered_from":"c9c8a905f98e1b692a1b0264c2072d57eefba163a815f7197401449f8d842bf2","blob":"6c75605d250c7c354f4e68ef2c88ecd2453ef75d","intervals":[[84,84]],"path":".github/workflows/ratchet-propose.yml"},"target":"33fed6c11891155e4ab31460815ed8fb9d075483"},"finding_id":"a56cb9d20d1ea8be215cf88d816837475a55ad245059a434b9e3aacd5a963ebe","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"5b1666510470f3c3b6f3a0dcc6b7c951542c7fe9253e129e9f762fbe81af585a"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:a56cb9d20d1ea8be215cf88d816837475a55ad245059a434b9e3aacd5a963ebe:ab337408d08a284da58f5f6f83a801c3a6419d8c691695c6270333eea0de0962"}